module product.data_category

import std.types { String }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }

// THE HANDLING-CLASS MARKERS, ONE ROW EACH, AND NOTHING ELSE. A category here names a class of data
// the product handles -- it is the C in product.data_class Classified<C, T> -- and it GRANTS
// NOTHING: which sinks a category may reach, under which lawful basis, kept for how long, and in
// whose scope, are rows of the data-handling map, which is private policy and is never enumerated
// in this tree (parent ruling msg_144d9121, point 4: the marker identifies the handling class; the
// grant lives on the sink and the permit). So "PersonalIdentity" never reads as "permitted".
//
// OPEN BY ROW, NOT A CLOSED ENUM. Each category is its own bare type declaration, so a category is
// added by adding a declaration and its private description row, not by widening a coproduct every
// match would then have to re-eliminate. std.magnitude Magnitude is the same shape: a nominal
// identity with no inhabitant, consulted only as a type argument.
//
// ONE ROSTER, TWO HALVES (DESIGN 3, agreed with the M2 compliance lane 2026-09-13). The marker is
// public and type-level; the DESCRIPTION -- what we process under it, where, for what purpose,
// under which basis, with what ratification standing -- is gunbc-private strategy.data_map, whose
// rows cite these declarations by DeclarationRef { module_path: "product.data_category", decl_name }.
// The eight markers below are one per description row, under the same names that lane authors.
// The join is walled on the citing side, by a cited-declaration-exists witness; nothing here copies
// that lane's names.
//
// THE SCOPE EXCLUSION IS EXPRESSED BY ABSENCE. The private map states an explicit exclusion: no
// end-user personal data. PersonalIdentity names the identity of an ACCOUNT or ADMIN principal --
// the person who signed in -- and there is deliberately no EndUserPersonalData marker: a category
// with no marker has no Classified constructor, no sink row and no permit, which is the type-level
// form of "we do not hold it".

type PersonalIdentity
type SourceAndBuildInput
type BuildOutput
type CiSecret
type JobLog
type MeteringTelemetry
type SupportCommunication
type AbuseAndSanctionsRecord

// THE RUNTIME NAME OF EACH MARKER. A type argument has no value at run time, and the interpretation
// path does not yet judge marker identity at generic positions (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode
// generic_application_admits_distinct_unit_variant_arguments and its bare-marker sibling), so
// every Classified value and every Sink also carries the marker's declaration reference, and the
// admission fold compares those. These are the only spellings of the references; a consumer that
// needs one imports it rather than re-spelling the module path. A marker gains its reference
// function with its FIRST MINT OR SINK, so no function here is a declaration nothing reads
// (DESIGN 3c, review 65204). PersonalIdentity and BuildOutput earned theirs from their mints. The
// remaining six earn theirs from the first SINK: gunbc-private strategy.data_map binds one marker
// per description row and hands it to product.data_class admit_data_effect, which compares marker
// identity -- so without these the private rows would have to re-spell the module path, forking the
// only spelling this annotation exists to keep single (DESIGN 3).
//
// THIS SENTENCE PREVIOUSLY SAID ONLY TWO REFERENCES EXIST, and it stood above two while the corpus
// needed eight. Prose asserting what the code contradicts rots silently because no Accepted program
// can read it (DESIGN 4c); the count is gone from this annotation for that reason -- the functions
// below are the census.
data data_category_module_path: String = "product.data_category"

fn personal_identity_ref() -> DeclarationRef { decl_ref(module_path: data_category_module_path, decl_name: "PersonalIdentity") }
fn build_output_ref() -> DeclarationRef { decl_ref(module_path: data_category_module_path, decl_name: "BuildOutput") }
fn source_and_build_input_ref() -> DeclarationRef { decl_ref(module_path: data_category_module_path, decl_name: "SourceAndBuildInput") }
fn ci_secret_ref() -> DeclarationRef { decl_ref(module_path: data_category_module_path, decl_name: "CiSecret") }
fn job_log_ref() -> DeclarationRef { decl_ref(module_path: data_category_module_path, decl_name: "JobLog") }
fn metering_telemetry_ref() -> DeclarationRef { decl_ref(module_path: data_category_module_path, decl_name: "MeteringTelemetry") }
fn support_communication_ref() -> DeclarationRef { decl_ref(module_path: data_category_module_path, decl_name: "SupportCommunication") }
fn abuse_and_sanctions_record_ref() -> DeclarationRef { decl_ref(module_path: data_category_module_path, decl_name: "AbuseAndSanctionsRecord") }
